  "_comment": "🧩️ This subset's own contribution to the repository test platform — the HTML 5 `any` mutation vocabulary and the reference implementation that exercises it. `html5ever`/`markup5ever_rcdom` are registered here under a distinct id and the `html-5-mutate` capability this subset's exhaustive mutation case (`mutate-html-5`) actually tags, per the wave 7 fleet brief's oracle-registration gotcha (reusing a neighbour's entry fails the contract with `oracle-capability-mismatch`).",
  "oracles": [
    {
      "id": "html5ever-html-5-mutate",
      "ecosystem": "rust",
      "package": "html5ever",
      "version": "0.39",
      "capabilities": [
        "html-5-mutate"
      ],
      "comparisonProfiles": [
        "semantic-html-v1"
      ],
      "license": "MIT OR Apache-2.0",
      "testOnly": true,
      "homepage": "https://github.com/servo/html5ever",
      "rationale": "🩹️ RECLASSIFIED (ticket SEPARATE-ARTIFACT-STANDARD-SUBSET-IMPLEMENTATIONS-AND-FIXTURE-TEST-EVERY-MUTATION, shard A10, 2026-09-02). This entry was registered `third-party-library` on the strength of a real crate that does genuine codec work, but the mutation's expected RESULT is computed by this owner's own `🦀️oracle.rs` -- its dispatch function's catch-all arm is `\"mutation kind {...} has no oracle implementation\"`, proof that every OTHER arm is an implementation, not a reading. Both halves of the comparison then descend from the same specification, so a shared misreading produces two agreeing wrong answers -- the one failure a differential oracle exists to catch. This is a `cross-semio-implementation`: a required SUPPLEMENT (metamorphic/inverse/round-trip evidence), never a substitute. A qualifying third-party reference for the mutation semantics is still owed. See $TICKET/📓️a10-oracle-honesty.md.\n\nThe WHATWG-conformant HTML5 tokenizer/tree-builder of the Rust ecosystem, paired with the reference-counted DOM `markup5ever_rcdom` 0.39 (MIT OR Apache-2.0, a companion crate from the same project, also test-only, https://github.com/servo/html5ever/tree/main/rcdom) — `html5ever` only tokenizes and builds a tree via a caller-supplied `TreeSink`, so it is not usable as a mutation oracle without it. Registered under `html5ever` because every scenario's comparison runs through `html5ever::parse_document` as the independent reader on BOTH sides (oracle output and subject output alike), matching how this catalog's `@oracle-` tag names a single id per feature; `markup5ever_rcdom` supplies the `RcDom`/`SerializableHandle` every one of those parses and re-serializes builds on, and is exercised by every green scenario even though it is not the package name on this entry; it is declared in this entry's `packages` list, which is what puts it inside the same test-only ratchet and oracle-purity probe as `html5ever` instead of being documented in prose alone. Together the only registered pair that both PARSES real, error-recovering HTML5 and WRITES it back out, so it can independently produce a second result for every one of this subset's 10 `HtmlMutation` kinds rather than merely reading.",
      "hostPath": "✏️s/🔌️plugins/🗄️stdio/🧪️oracle/📦️packages/🦀️rust",
      "packages": [
        {
          "package": "markup5ever_rcdom",
          "version": "0.39",
          "license": "MIT OR Apache-2.0",
          "homepage": "https://github.com/servo/html5ever/tree/main/rcdom",
          "role": "reference-counted DOM tree sink and serializer — the tree `html5ever` only builds through a caller-supplied TreeSink"
        }
      ],
